This repository contains code copied from UmbraDB (https://github.com/midnightntwrk/umbradb), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE, identical to UmbraDB's):

- gpu/device.ts, gpu/ipir.ts, gpu/ipir-wgsl.ts, gpu/ipir-wire.ts (from examples/private-shielded-sync/gpu/) and
  ipir/sizes.ts (from examples/private-shielded-sync/ipir/), at commit
  c620f0e76db4e5d78001eb3dc3a45363c10f47da ("examples/private-shielded-sync/gpu: IPIR+SP's answer on the GPU, byte
  for byte as the add-on's", 2026-11-16). gpu/ipir.ts is changed in this repository: GpuIpirTable.create also takes
  cells and packing matrices that are already in GPU buffers, and createEmpty and writeBlock are added, for a table
  filled one column block at a time. The other four files are unchanged;
- ipir/vendor/ and ipir/Cargo.lock (adapted), from examples/private-shielded-sync/ipir/ at commit
  4f362386a1b6fbbf041cceed92f8fba432ee2600.

ipir/vendor/ipir-sp/ holds five crates of the IPIR+SP repository of the Zcash wallet services
(https://github.com/valargroup/ipir-sp, commit 791b5287a26e4fe021f6f1a8fe70b7ab23849787), each licensed
MIT OR Apache-2.0 (ipir/vendor/ORIGIN.md, ipir/vendor/LICENSE-MIT, ipir/vendor/LICENSE-APACHE), with four patches
applied (ipir/patches/README.md describes each):

- ipir/patches/0001-setup-without-columns.patch, this design's: a table gains column blocks and keeps the ones it has;
- ipir/patches/0002-faster-block-compile.patch: a faster CPU block compile with the same output words;
- ipir/patches/0003-gpu-build-accessors.patch: read-only accessors for a build of a column block on the GPU;
- ipir/patches/0004-first-pass-hook.patch: additions for timing a whole answer with the CUDA kernel, and the CUDA
  release of the bindings as a build feature.

